<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>IECEx Certificate of Conformity</title>
<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  .page {
    width: 794px; height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, "DejaVu Sans", "Liberation Sans";
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 15px; }
  td { padding: 5px 0; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="page">
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <div>
      <img src="placeholder_iec_logo.png" alt="IEC Logo" style="height: 50px; margin-right: 10px;">
      <img src="placeholder_iecex_logo.png" alt="IECEx Logo" style="height: 50px;">
    </div>
    <div style="text-align: right;">
      <h1 style="font-size: 24pt; margin: 0;">IECEx Certificate of Conformity</h1>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 40px;">
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">INTERNATIONAL ELECTROTECHNICAL COMMISSION</p>
    <p style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold;">IEC Certification System for Explosive Atmospheres</p>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">for rules and details of the IECEx Scheme visit www.iecex.com</p>
  </div>

  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 30px; font-size: 10pt;">
    <div>
      <p>Certificate No.: <span data-field="certificate_no">{{ certificate_no }}</span></p>
      <p>Status: <span data-field="status">{{ status }}</span></p>
      <p>Date of Issue: <span data-field="date_of_issue">{{ date_of_issue }}</span></p>
      <p>Applicant: <span data-field="applicant_name">{{ applicant.name }}</span></p>
      <p>Equipment: <span data-field="equipment_description">{{ equipment.description }}</span></p>
      <p>Optional accessory: <span data-field="optional_accessory">{{ optional_accessory }}</span></p>
      <p>Type of Protection: <span data-field="type_of_protection">{{ type_of_protection }}</span></p>
      <p>Marking: <span data-field="marking">{{ marking }}</span></p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p>Page <span data-field="page_number">{{ page_number }}</span> of <span data-field="total_pages">{{ total_pages }}</span></p>
      <p>Issue No: <span data-field="issue_no">{{ issue_no }}</span></p>
      <p>Certificate History: <span data-field="certificate_history">{{ certificate_history }}</span></p>
      <p>Issue No: <span data-field="issue_no_2">{{ issue_no_2 }}</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 50px;">
    <div style="width: 45%;">
      <p>Approved for issue on behalf of the IECEx Certification Body:</p>
      <p style="margin-top: 50px;">Signature:</p>
      <p style="font-size: 9pt;">(for printed version)</p>
      <p>Date: <span data-field="date_signed">{{ date_signed }}</span></p>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 45%; text-align: right;">
      <p>R S Sinclair</p>
      <p style="margin-top: 50px;">Technical Manager</p>
      <div style="border-bottom: 1px solid black; width: 150px; margin-top: 50px;"></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <div>
      <img src="placeholder_iec_logo.png" alt="IEC Logo" style="height: 50px; margin-right: 10px;">
      <img src="placeholder_iecex_logo.png" alt="IECEx Logo" style="height: 50px;">
    </div>
    <div style="text-align: right;">
      <h1 style="font-size: 24pt; margin: 0;">IECEx Certificate of Conformity</h1>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 30px; font-size: 10pt;">
    <div>
      <p>Certificate No.: <span data-field="certificate_no_2">{{ certificate_no_2 }}</span></p>
      <p>Date of Issue: <span data-field="date_of_issue_2">{{ date_of_issue_2 }}</span></p>
      <p>Manufacturer: <span data-field="manufacturer_name">{{ manufacturer.name }}</span></p>
      <p>Additional manufacturing locations: <span data-field="additional_locations">{{ additional_locations }}</span></p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p>Page <span data-field="page_number_2">{{ page_number_2 }}</span> of <span data-field="total_pages_2">{{ total_pages_2 }}</span></p>
      <p>Issue No: <span data-field="issue_no_2_2">{{ issue_no_2_2 }}</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <p>This certificate is issued as verification that a sample(s), representative of production, was assessed and tested and found to comply with the requirements of the IECEx Certification Scheme. This certificate is granted subject to the conditions as set out in the IECEx Scheme Rules, IECEx O2 and Operational Documents as amended.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <p><strong>STANDARDS:</strong></p>
    <p>The equipment and any acceptable variations to it specified in the schedule of this certificate and the identified documents, was found to comply with the following standards:</p>
    <table>
      <tr>
        <td style="width: 30%;">IEC <span data-field="standard_1">{{ standard_1 }}</span></td>
        <td style="width: 70%;">Explosive atmospheres - Part 0: General requirements</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Edition: <span data-field="edition_1">{{ edition_1 }}</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>IEC <span data-field="standard_2">{{ standard_2 }}</span></td>
        <td>Explosive atmospheres - Part 11: Equipment protection by intrinsic safety "i"</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Edition: <span data-field="edition_2">{{ edition_2 }}</span></td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <p>This Certificate does not indicate compliance with safety and performance requirements other than those expressly included in the Standards listed above.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <p><strong>TEST & ASSESSMENT REPORTS:</strong></p>
    <p>A sample(s) of the equipment listed has successfully met the examination and test requirements as recorded in:</p>
    <table>
      <tr>
        <td style="width: 33%;">Test Reports: <span data-field="test_report_1">{{ test_report_1 }}</span></td>
        <td style="width: 33%;">Test Reports: <span data-field="test_report_2">{{ test_report_2 }}</span></td>
        <td style="width: 33%;">Test Reports: <span data-field="test_report_3">{{ test_report_3 }}</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Quality Assessment Report: <span data-field="quality_assessment_report">{{ quality_assessment_report }}</span></td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <div>
      <img src="placeholder_iec_logo.png" alt="IEC Logo" style="height: 50px; margin-right: 10px;">
      <img src="placeholder_iecex_logo.png" alt="IECEx Logo" style="height: 50px;">
    </div>
    <div style="text-align: right;">
      <h1 style="font-size: 24pt; margin: 0;">IECEx Certificate of Conformity</h1>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 30px; font-size: 10pt;">
    <div>
      <p>Certificate No.: <span data-field="certificate_no_3">{{ certificate_no_3 }}</span></p>
      <p>Date of Issue: <span data-field="date_of_issue_3">{{ date_of_issue_3 }}</span></p>
      <p>Issue No: <span data-field="issue_no_3">{{ issue_no_3 }}</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <p><strong>EQUIPMENT:</strong></p>
    <p>Equipment and systems covered by this Certificate are as follows:</p>
    <p>The <span data-field="equipment_name_3">{{ equipment_name_3 }}</span> and <span data-field="equipment_name_4">{{ equipment_name_4 }}</span> are devices for measuring the pH level or Oxidation-Reduction Potential of a process medium. The sensors are available in a standard model and a "Hot Tap" model. The difference between the models is enclosure type and connection type.</p>
    <p>The <span data-field="equipment_name_5">{{ equipment_name_5 }}</span> models are covered by this certificate as described by the part number/ordering code as follows:</p>
    <p>The equipment is formed of a moulded plastic enclosure that is resistant to most aggressive substances. The sensing part of the assembly is glass part that may be curved (bulllet shaped) or flat. The glass is either filled with a conductive liquid or empty depending on the application.</p>
    <p>The pH and ORP sensors are differentiated by the glass bullet or flat sensing head used. The pH sensor can be identified by means of a colouration of the glass that may or may not be present and, more importantly, no wiring passing through the surface of the glass. The ORP sensor can be identified by means of a colouration of the glass that may or may not be present and, more importantly, no wiring passing through the surface of the glass.</p>
    <p>Electrical connections are then made to either the plug and socket arrangement or directly to the barrier via a coaxial cable to a maximum length of 10 m.</p>
    <p>The sensor is exposed, in its end-use application, a process medium that may have a maximum pressure of up to and including 10 bar.</p>
    <p>The <span data-field="equipment_name_6">{{ equipment_name_6 }}</span> sensors are barrier powered device considered against the level of protection "ia" with the following input entity and load parameters:</p>
    <table>
      <tr>
        <td style="width: 20%;">Ui: <span data-field="ui_6">{{ ui_6 }}</span></td>
        <td style="width: 20%;">Ie: <span data-field="ie_6">{{ ie_6 }}</span></td>
        <td style="width: 20%;">C1: <span data-field="c1_6">{{ c1_6 }}</span></td>
        <td style="width: 20%;">C2: <span data-field="c2_6">{{ c2_6 }}</span></td>
        <td style="width: 20%;">P1: <span data-field="p1_6">{{ p1_6 }}</span></td>
      </tr>
    </table>
    <p>Optional accessories allow for a metallic sheath to be used in conjunction with the sensor. The metallic sheath element is not covered under the scope of this certificate.</p>
    <p>For a nomenclature breakdown of the products covered by this certificate refer to the attached Annex.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 40px;">
    <p><strong>SPECIFIC CONDITIONS OF USE:</strong> YES as shown below:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>The plastic enclosure is a potential electrostatic hazard. Clean only with a damp cloth and do not mount in a high velocity dust laden atmosphere.</li>
      <li>The stainless steel threaded connector is a potential electrostatic hazard. Ensure that the earth connection on the connector is provided with an earth connection as described in the instructions.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <div>
      <img src="placeholder_iec_logo.png" alt="IEC Logo" style="height: 50px; margin-right: 10px;">
      <img src="placeholder_iecex_logo.png" alt="IECEx Logo" style="height: 50px;">
    </div>
    <div style="text-align: right;">
      <h1 style="font-size: 24pt; margin: 0;">IECEx Certificate of Conformity</h1>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 30px; font-size: 10pt;">
    <div>
      <p>Certificate No.: <span data-field="certificate_no_4">{{ certificate_no_4 }}</span></p>
      <p>Date of Issue: <span data-field="date_of_issue_4">{{ date_of_issue_4 }}</span></p>
      <p>Issue No: <span data-field="issue_no_4">{{ issue_no_4 }}</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <p><strong>DETAILS OF CERTIFICATE CHANGES (for issues 1 and above)</strong></p>
    <table>
      <tr>
        <td style="width: 30%;">Variation 2.1</td>
        <td style="width: 70%;">To permit an increase to the maximum input current (Ii) and maximum input power (Pi) described in the terminal parameters to 100 mA and 600 mW respectively.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>ExtR: <span data-field="extr_code">{{ extr_code }}</span></td>
        <td>File Reference: <span data-field="file_reference">{{ file_reference }}</span></td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <p>Annex:</p>
    <p><span data-field="annex_file">{{ annex_file }}</span></p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <div style="width: 50%;">
      <p>SGS Baseefa Limited</p>
      <p>Rockhead Business Park</p>
      <p>Staden Lane</p>
      <p>Buxton, Derbyshire, SK17 9RZ</p>
      <p>United Kingdom</p>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 50%; text-align: right;">
      <img src="placeholder_sgs_logo.png" alt="SGS Logo" style="max-width: 300px;">
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <p>ANNEX to IECEx BAS <span data-field="annex_certificate_no">{{ annex_certificate_no }}</span> Issue No. 0</p>
    <p>Date: <span data-field="annex_date">{{ annex_date }}</span></p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <p><strong>Annex A.1 – 500 PRO-D and 500 PRO-D HT Digital pH/ORP sensors</strong> are devices for measuring the pH level or Oxidation-Reduction Potential of a process medium. The sensor is available in a standard model and a "Hot Tap" model. The difference between the models is enclosure shape and application.</p>
    <p>The 500 PRO-D models covered by this certificate are described by the part number/ordering code as follows:</p>
    <table>
      <tr>
        <td style="width: 10%;">I</td>
        <td style="width: 10%;">II</td>
        <td style="width: 10%;">III</td>
        <td style="width: 10%;">IV</td>
        <td style="width: 10%;">V</td>
        <td style="width: 50%;"></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Where:</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>I signifies the model reference;</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>II signifies the sensor type and may be P2 (pH Sensor - general purpose bullet shaped glass), P4 (pH Sensor - low resistance and temperature glass), P5 (pH Sensor - high resistance and temperature glass), P6 (pH Sensor - high performance, coating resistant and high temperature glass) or R2 (ORP Sensor - high resistance and temperature glass).</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>III signifies the body type and may be K1 for a 3/4" threaded insertion/immersion - no sensor guard (flush) or K2 for a 3/4" threaded insertion/immersion - notched sensor guard.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>IV signifies the connection type and is a D relating to a EZLink Digital Connection.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>V signifies integrated cable length and may be 00 (No integrated cable) - only available with the VarioPin Option), 01 (0 m integrated cable), 03 (3 m integrated cable), 05 (5 m integrated cable) or 10 (10 m integrated cable).</td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <p>The 500 PRO-D HT models covered by this certificate are described by the part number/ordering code as follows:</p>
    <table>
      <tr>
        <td style="width: 10%;">I</td>
        <td style="width: 10%;">II</td>
        <td style="width: 10%;">III</td>
        <td style="width: 10%;">IV</td>
        <td style="width: 10%;">V</td>
        <td style="width: 10%;">VI</td>
        <td style="width: 40%;"></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Where:</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>I signifies the model reference;</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>II signifies the sensor type and may be P2 (pH Sensor - general purpose bullet shaped glass), P4 (pH Sensor - low resistance and temperature glass), P5 (pH Sensor - high resistance and temperature glass), P6 (pH Sensor - high performance, coating resistant and high temperature glass) or R2 (ORP Sensor - high resistance and temperature glass).</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>III signifies the body type and may be K3 for a hot-tap ball valve insertion - notched sensor guard (flush) or K4 for a hot-tap ball valve insertion - notched sensor guard.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>IV signifies the connection type and is a D relating to a EZLink Digital Connection.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>V signifies integrated cable length and may be 01 (0 m integrated cable), 03 (3 m integrated cable), 05 (5 m integrated cable) or 10 (10 m integrated cable).</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>VI signifies the connection type and is a D relating to a EZLink Digital Connection.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>VII signifies integrated cable length and may be 01 (0 m integrated cable), 03 (3 m integrated cable), 05 (5 m integrated cable) or 10 (10 m integrated cable).</td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>